- **Line 67 — idempotency guard satisfied by marker, not work.**  
  Exact input: `x_REVIEW.html` containing:
  ```html
  <!-- Math.abs(_gUCI - _gLCI) -->
                  const ciWidth = (_gLCI > 0 && _gUCI > 0) ? Math.log(_gUCI) - Math.log(_gLCI) : Infinity;
  ```
  Consequence: the buggy `ciWidth` line is skipped forever and reported as unchanged.

- **Line 73 — occurrence-count defect.**  
  Exact input: `x_REVIEW.html` containing the line below twice:
  ```js
                  const ciWidth = (_gLCI > 0 && _gUCI > 0) ? Math.log(_gUCI) - Math.log(_gLCI) : Infinity;
  ```
  Consequence: only the first occurrence is fixed, then the inserted `Math.abs(...)` marker makes later runs skip the file with the second buggy occurrence still present.

- **Line 81 — check/status cannot fail for missed work.**  
  Exact input: `RAPIDMETA_REPO_ROOT` set to a directory containing `x_REVIEW.html` with:
  ```js
  const ciWidth = (_gLCI>0 && _gUCI>0) ? Math.log(_gUCI)-Math.log(_gLCI) : Infinity;
  ```
  Consequence: no replacement happens, but the process still exits `0`, so a caller cannot distinguish “fixed/not needed” from “selector missed the defect.”

- **Lines 66 and 76 — line endings compared/written as text.**  
  Exact input: on Windows, an LF-only `x_REVIEW.html` containing one exact old replacement line.  
  Consequence: applying the fix rewrites the file through text mode and can convert LF to CRLF, creating unrelated full-file diff noise.

